The guarantee of k147 for the other two harnesses: wherever a Codex or Hermes session works in a skilletor project, that checkout has its declared items, with no `skilletor sync` by hand. Neither has a `CwdChanged` event, so each needs its own place to notice the move.

## Codex (codex-cli 0.153.4 on reuben)

Hook events in the binary: SessionStart, SessionEnd, UserPromptSubmit, PreToolUse, PostToolUse, PermissionRequest, PreCompact, PostCompact, SubagentStart, SubagentStop, TurnStart, Stop. skilletor's `hooks/codex-hooks.json` uses SessionStart and UserPromptSubmit.

Establish first, by measurement: can a Codex session or one of its subagents end up working in another checkout than the one SessionStart synced? Candidates: the exec tools' per-call `workdir` (the session cwd itself seems fixed), a persistent shell (`write_stdin`) after `cd`, SubagentStart's input `cwd`, briefing's Codex resolution (`codex_layers(cwd)` in `briefing-preload`). If yes: hook the event that sees it (SubagentStart, PreToolUse/PostToolUse, TurnStart) and bring that checkout up to date as k147 does. If no: the docs say why Codex needs nothing beyond SessionStart, with the measurement on this card.

## Hermes Agent

Hermes keeps a working directory per session (`tools/terminal_tool.py`: `record_session_cwd` / `get_session_cwd`), so a `cd` moves the session like in Claude Code. Plugin hooks include `pre_tool_call`, `post_tool_call`, `pre_llm_call`, `subagent_start`, `on_session_start` (`hermes_cli/plugins.py` `VALID_HOOKS`). The adapter `hermes/skilletor/__init__.py` registers `on_session_start` and `pre_llm_call` and takes the project from `agent.runtime_cwd.resolve_agent_cwd()`.

Establish whether that cwd follows a `cd` in the terminal tool and when Hermes resolves project skills (`.hermes/skills/`). Then: on a move into another checkout of a skilletor project (noticed in `post_tool_call` of the terminal tool, or at the latest in the next `pre_llm_call`), bring it up to date and report the line as k147 does. Test Hermes: `~/dev/hermes-citiai/.dev/` (venv, hermes-agent checkout from 2026-10-03 — compare with current upstream before relying on an API). Always set `HERMES_HOME` to a temp dir; enable plugins via `plugins.enabled` in its `config.yaml`, never `hermes plugins enable` in a throwaway home (pulls 500 MB into `$HERMES_HOME/cache/uv`).

